Hi, all,
In the following condition in tools/tpm2_loadexternal.c, if both policy and=
 auth are empty, then it will also set TPMA_OBJECT_USERWITHAUTH.
Seems it is not correct.
    pub.publicArea.objectAttributes =3D BASE_DEFAULT_ATTRS;
    if (!(ctx.policy && !ctx.auth)) {
        pub.publicArea.objectAttributes |=3D TPMA_OBJECT_USERWITHAUTH;
    }

And no description about  this scenario in spec, part2, section 8.3.1.
6

userWithAuth

SET (1): Approval of USER role actions with this object may be with an HMAC=
 session or with a password using the authValue of the object or a policy s=
ession.
CLEAR (0): Approval of USER role actions with this object may only be done =
with a policy session.


Can you help to give more information?

Thanks.

  *   Shirley

